# Hosting and /api/analyze

Hosting serves `dist`. Rewrite `/api/analyze` to Cloud Function `analyze` in `asia-northeast3`, then `**` → `/index.html`. Hashed `/assets/**` may be immutable; HTML is `no-cache`.

The client always `fetch("/api/analyze")` with the user JWT. Same path on Firebase and Netlify.

- Firebase: [`functions/src/index.ts`](functions/src/index.ts), `process.env`
- Netlify: [`netlify/functions/analyze.ts`](netlify/functions/analyze.ts), `Netlify.env.get`

Both verify Supabase `getUser`, then Anthropic. On 401/503 the client uses `src/lib/tagger.ts`. 2nd-gen functions need Blaze; Spark Hosting still ships the SPA.

Function env (never Vite): `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `SUPABASE_URL` or `VITE_SUPABASE_URL`, `SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` or `VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`. Keep `functions/.env` gitignored.

Deploy Hosting: `npx -y firebase-tools@latest deploy --only hosting` (or `npm run deploy:hosting`). Live: `https://mybrary-snuu09.web.app`.
